"53. Cell U6 (g) at rank 2, second lane: closure of Gram positivity under symmetric Blaschke insertions. `c17-rank2-gram-symmetric-blaschke-closure` (one referee; partial result) and `c18-d10-inertia-law-theorem-t-lemma-d` (one referee; partial result). Kind: neither proved nor refuted; the form is rank-one Maass-Selberg plus one apex kernel that reads the pole at 1 and the reflection symmetry of the zero set; a symmetric off-line quartet passes (Theorem Q in the rational model, exact; 600 of 600 on the zeta base); X(d) is proved for d = 2, 4 only; the parity clause of the round-17 inertia law holds in the model with b = u (u - 1) g. State: tried, not closed; a record item only (the row cannot score whatever X(d) gives); round-19 lane `c19-d10-xd-determinant-pole-term-lemma-q`. [D10, round-17 revision and round-18 addendum]",
