"55. Device type `tz-one-sided-completion-bound-band` (the input named by item 51: N(theta) for 1/2 < theta <= 1 with the reflected half of the approximate functional equation as completion). `c18-tz-one-sided-bound-fe-reserve-bridge` (paper; one referee, E1 to E7) and `c18-tz-band-completion-controls-server` (heavy compute; one referee, E1 to E6): two refereed obstructions. Kind: by an exact truncation identity valid for every Dirichlet series with a_1 = 1, N(theta) below the Nyquist band is a statement about zeros of the partial sum D_P (no R1); ZQ passes for theta' < 1 in the lattice model and sign chains, E_0.1 and DH pass on 96 modes in parts of the band (no R3); at theta' = 1 it is the target (no R4); the linear reflected completion is not a positive extension (zeta fails it in 600 of 600 cells). The measured passes depend on the number of modes. State: closed in the device table; the continuation on file is a completion positive by construction with pre-registered mode counts (round-19 lane `c19-rs-real-zero-completion-band-server`). [P58]",
